WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.160
Hey! Are you seriously
never going to sing again?

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.800
I'll transform you as many
times as you want!

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:12.960
She's not transforming!

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:14.600
Why?

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:16.960
Unless Mitsuki has the desire,

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.700
we won't be able to transform her
with our Death Spirit powers.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.100
No way.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:26.730
Mitsuki...

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:11.860
IS FULL MOON RETIRING AT LAST?!

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:17.530
<i>Full Moon...</i>
<i>What in the world is up with her?</i>

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:20.500
Madoka, it's time for rehearsal.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:21.560
Okay!

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.430
- Good morning!
- Good morning!

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:25.530
Good morning!

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:31.830
Hey, hey, have you heard the news?
Full Moon is finally retiring.

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:36.400
Yeah, I heard that the record company
is already searching for a new artist.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:38.930
Really? Maybe I'll bring
them a demo tape!

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.260
What? Now?!

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:41.330
Hey!

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:44.460
Do me a favor and stop
spreading random rumors!

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.230
There's no way she'd retire!

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.760
Full Moon isn't the kind of girl
who would give up that easily!

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.200
Got it?!

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:52.860
Oh... Yes.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.300
Madoka...

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:57.530
Gimme a break!
Running off their mouths like that!

00:02:57.960 --> 00:02:59.530
I don't know what
it is with you,

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:02.660
but I suggest you do something about
that strong-headed manner of speaking.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:05.300
I take after you in strong-headedness.

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:16.500
Oh, Ms. Oshige!

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.160
Oh, Ms. Imamura.

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:22.300
What are you doing here today?
Full Moon is off, right?

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:27.260
Yes. I came to pick up the fan letters
that were sent here to the program.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:29.000
Oh, I see.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.660
<i>- If I remember correctly,</i>
- Please give her my best regards too.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:32.100
<i>that woman is</i>
<i>Full Moon's manager.</i>

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.730
Thank you.
Well, see you.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:39.160
Ms. Imamura...

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.200
Yes? What is it?

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:42.430
What's my schedule for today?

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:44.760
You're free for
the rest of the day.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:45.860
Great!

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:46.560
Huh?

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.300
Nothing. Thank you!

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:53.800
<i>If I trail her, I might be</i>
<i>able to find out something.</i>

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.360
Hey! If you don't hurry,
I'll leave you behind!

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:12.900
<i>Yes?</i>

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.330
It's Oshige.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.800
Kamiyama?

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:21.960
This is Full Moon's house?

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:25.760
I see, so they've
gone to the hospital.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:28.860
I'm sorry that you went
out of your way to visit.

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:32.000
It's no problem.
I'll come by again another day.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:41.600
She still has the fan letters.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:51.460
Maybe it wasn't here after all.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:01.660
Huh?

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:07.530
<i>That's that girl from back then.</i>

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.930
So this is that girl's house?

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.200
Are you tired?

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:22.660
Yes.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:31.100
Mitsuki, you must eat for
the sake of your health.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:33.130
Okay.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:37.230
Do you think you can
eat something today?

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:44.100
I'll bring you some fruit later.

00:05:58.230 --> 00:05:59.230
Ms. Tanaka.

00:05:59.260 --> 00:05:59.930
Yes?

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.200
Please bring Mitsuki
some fruit later.

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:04.430
Yes.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:08.430
Umm... Ma'am?

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:10.130
What is it?

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.360
How was the hospital?

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:17.260
M-Ma'am?

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:31.430
Did you find it?

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:37.700
Who are those guys?

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:48.560
Hey!

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:52.400
Oh, Takuto! Where were you,
slacking off like that?

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:54.630
More importantly, look at that.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:58.730
Hey, hey.

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:02.030
Madoka Wakamatsu? Why?!

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:09.000
Hey, you!

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:12.460
Madoka?

00:07:13.230 --> 00:07:14.930
Can I come in?
I can, right?

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:21.300
Sorry!

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:27.830
I was so surprised to see you here!
I couldn't help but say hello!

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:33.900
Are you not feeling well?
Do you have a fever?

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:38.260
Oh, you don't have a fever!

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:44.230
Am I bothering you?
Do you want me to leave?

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:46.260
No.

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:50.000
I didn't think so! After all,
you're a fan of mine, right?

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:53.830
You must be thrilled because I came
to visit you when you're sick, right?

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:04.960
<i>Dear Grandma, I met with</i>
<i>Dr. Herberd the other day.</i>

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:08.900
<i>I was very happy to hear that</i>
<i>I might recover from my illness.</i>

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:12.260
<i>The landscape here in America</i>
<i>is very expansive</i>

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:15.000
<i>and it makes me</i>
<i>feel very small.</i>

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:18.430
<i>Next time, I'd like to come</i>
<i>here with you, Grandma.</i>

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:19.760
<i>Mitsuki.</i>

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:31.530
That song...
That's my song!

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:37.230
Well, I guess Full Moon
sings it too.

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:42.230
Speaking of, Full Moon's manager
dropped by this house.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.400
How do you know her?

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:49.660
You don't feel well, do you?

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.960
What happened to all that energy
you had that last time

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.960
when you were talking
so big to me?

00:08:56.730 --> 00:08:58.230
But it's really weird, isn't it?

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.630
That Full Moon has suddenly
taken time off from work.

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:07.930
You and Full Moon...

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:10.060
I was thinking that I wouldn't
be where I am today

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:12.360
if it hadn't been
for both of you.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:14.600
You probably wouldn't
understand this,

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:18.000
but Full Moon is a girl
who really pisses me off.

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:20.260
She seems to be
so full of confidence.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:23.260
I'm looking forward to
knocking her down someday.

00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:25.900
Do you understand
what I mean?

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:29.100
What I'm saying is that if
Full Moon weren't around,

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:31.860
I would lose sight of what
I'm aspiring to right now.

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:36.230
So that's how Madoka
sees Full Moon.

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:42.000
So it seems. In those days this girl
was so strong it even surprised us.

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:47.430
And moreover,
I'd really be depressed

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:53.330
if a cheeky girl like you who told me
that I have my own song lost her vitality.

00:09:58.660 --> 00:09:59.660
Madoka...

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:01.130
Huh? What? What?

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:05.060
Full Moon...no longer exists.

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:07.000
Huh?

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:12.300
Come on... Don't talk nonsense!
Hurry up and get well.

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:15.730
Is there anything I can do?
Shall I sing you a song?

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:20.430
Mitsuki!

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:23.330
What's the matter?
Are you all right?

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:27.230
Mitsuki, are you all right?

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:31.000
I'm so sorry!
I invited myself in.

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:33.860
Hey, hang in there!

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:45.360
Mitsuki, be strong!

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:46.930
Ma'am?

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.000
U-Umm...

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:52.700
They're asking whether
you have a regular hospital.

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:54.600
A regular hospital?

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:59.060
<i>Dr. Wakaoji, I cannot entrust her</i>
<i>to you any longer.</i>

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:02.300
<i>From now on, please stay</i>
<i>out of our family's affairs.</i>

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:06.930
<i>Of course,</i>
<i>I will switch hospitals as well!</i>

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:16.730
Please take us to
Dr. Wakaoji's hospital!

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:33.630
Mitsuki, you'll be all right now!
You're at the hospital now!

00:11:33.930 --> 00:11:35.760
Doctor,
we're ready for her now.

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:37.060
All right.

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:39.360
Mitsuki...

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:48.400
<i>I am not in that girl's heart.</i>
<i>Isn't there anything I can do?</i>

00:11:49.030 --> 00:11:53.530
We must have Mitsuki
live out her life span!

00:11:54.430 --> 00:12:00.200
But it would be cruel to force her
to continue living in this state.

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:07.530
This is the first time I've had to
deal with...such an exhausting case.

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:09.100
That's not true!

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:11.800
Even if her life is short,

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:17.500
making her feel that it was worth living
is part of our job too, right?!

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:19.760
That hurts, Takuto!

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:26.260
Don't say such
irresponsible things!

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:28.230
That's impossible.

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:33.200
We're Death Spirits! There's no way
we would be able to do that!

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:38.360
Takuto, you idiot!

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:46.360
Ma'am, I will go get
her clothes and things.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:47.330
All right.

00:12:50.860 --> 00:12:51.530
Oh?

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:53.430
Umm... How is she?

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:55.530
It seems her condition
has stabilized.

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:56.560
What a relief.

00:12:56.700 --> 00:12:58.560
Well, I better go now.

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:02.530
You there.

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:06.860
I'm sorry about inviting myself in
to see your granddaughter.

00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:10.360
I had no idea that
she was that ill.

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:13.230
Are you a friend of
Mitsuki's from before?

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:16.660
Mitsuki?
I didn't know her name was Mitsuki.

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:25.130
I see. Is that what happened?

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:30.160
Yes. Thanks to Mitsuki,
I was inspired to persevere.

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:34.400
Until then I thought
I would quit singing, but...

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:41.560
<i>I think...that everyone</i>
<i>has a unique song.</i>

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:45.560
<i>There's a song for Full Moon.</i>

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:51.060
<i>But I think that there's also</i>
<i>a song that only you can sing.</i>

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:55.330
<i>I want to hear your song.</i>

00:13:57.530 --> 00:14:01.330
It made me think that if there is
somebody out there who says

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:03.700
they want to hear my song,
I should sing.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:06.960
It made me think that I should try
and persevere just a little longer.

00:14:07.460 --> 00:14:12.530
<i>Mitsuki's passion for song...</i>
<i>is what gave this girl strength.</i>

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:14.260
<i>Grandma...</i>

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:20.530
<i>Please listen to</i>
<i>my songs someday!</i>

00:14:21.860 --> 00:14:30.000
<i>I've never properly listened</i>
<i>to Mitsuki's singing.</i>

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:35.300
Dr. Wakaoji.

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:38.430
Mrs. Koyama...

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:44.530
Mitsuki... I beg you,
please help Mitsuki.

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:48.230
I will, with my body and soul.

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:50.760
I will do everything within
my power to help her.

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:55.730
Please, grant my request!

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:58.760
If you are going to that extent
to ask me, Wakaoji,

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:00.530
it will be risky for the hospital.

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:01.660
But let me try
to do something.

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:03.400
Thank you very much.

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:05.300
However,
there is one problem.

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:10.160
Our job is to cure people's
illnesses and save lives.

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:16.300
But unless the patient has
the desire to live or to get better

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:20.330
no matter how much effort we put into it
or how expensive our facilities are,

00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:21.930
we will not be able to
cure their illness.

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:23.230
Yes.

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:27.500
I will exert every possible effort
to give Mitsuki hope.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:35.560
<i>I do understand what</i>
<i>Meroko is saying.</i>

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:42.430
<i>There's no meaning in giving her</i>
<i>hope to live at this point,</i>

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:44.430
<i>when the span of her life</i>
<i>is almost up.</i>

00:15:45.760 --> 00:15:48.200
<i>But still, continuing this way</i>
<i>won't do either!</i>

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:49.860
<i>This is...</i>

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:55.130
<i>But...that girl's smiles</i>
<i>were all for Eichi.</i>

00:15:57.330 --> 00:16:00.100
<i>She was overflowing with</i>
<i>the desire to see Eichi.</i>

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:06.630
That idiot! He should have stayed alive
until he and Mitsuki reunited!

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:18.000
All those smiles were for you, Eichi.
So you... You can't die!

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:20.400
Damn it!

00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:24.730
Jeez... Why in the world did I
become a Death Spirit!

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:36.000
Th-There it is again!

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:42.430
What was that just now?
What happened to me?

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:48.000
What lovely flowers.

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:51.330
I'm so sorry.
She just fell asleep.

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:54.600
Don't worry about it.
I just dropped by to see how she was.

00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:57.830
I'm so relieved to see that
her condition has stabilized.

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:01.430
Get better soon, okay?

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.230
Well, I'll drop by again.

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:06.630
If you're leaving,
let me show you to the door.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:08.260
Don't worry about it!

00:17:08.530 --> 00:17:10.200
That's the least I can do.

00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:19.560
The two that you
were concerned about...

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:21.300
It looks like they're
doing all right now.

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:29.160
But...where did your heart go?
Did it freeze up in that snow?

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:34.860
Don't my words reach you?

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:41.760
Mitsuki... Wake up!
Please wake up and sing!

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:44.560
Let's sing together again
one more time, okay?

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:46.130
Okay, Mitsuki?!

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:18.230
W-Was that just now...
a memory of when I was alive?

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:21.630
<i>You understand what will</i>
<i>happen to you if you recover</i>

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:23.230
<i>your memory in this state,</i>
<i>don't you?</i>

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:27.630
<i>You will become a ghost</i>
<i>who wanders all alone.</i>

00:18:28.930 --> 00:18:31.060
Why am I remembering this
all of a sudden?

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:34.130
I didn't want to die!

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:36.230
I really didn't want to die!

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:41.200
Why is it?
Why am I feeling these things?

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:46.000
Why am I crying?
Why am I so sad?

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:49.930
What exactly did I do
when I was alive?!

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:54.800
Takuto?

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:01.700
What's the matter, Takuto?

00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:03.130
Shut up!

00:19:04.130 --> 00:19:05.700
Please leave me alone!

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:08.830
Takuto!

00:19:20.900 --> 00:19:24.000
What is...Takuto thinking?

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:28.030
I don't understand
what he's thinking.

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:35.300
<i>That's a lie.</i>
<i>I do understand.</i>

00:19:36.260 --> 00:19:42.000
<i>Even I know that</i>
<i>Takuto loves Mitsuki.</i>

00:19:48.060 --> 00:19:49.060
<i>It's so painful.</i>

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:56.000
<i>What don't you like about me?</i>
<i>Somebody tell me. Please!</i>

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:31.130
You're late, Mero.
I thought you would come sooner.

00:20:32.930 --> 00:20:35.830
I don't know
what's what anymore.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:40.930
Izumi, will you hear me out?

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:44.200
Of course, Mero.

00:20:49.660 --> 00:20:53.230
I never thought it would be so
painful to keep that girl alive

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:54.900
for the duration
of her life span.

00:20:56.160 --> 00:21:02.260
But Takuto doesn't understand
how I feel at all.

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:09.500
And...why are you hesitating?
That's not like you, Mero.

00:21:11.930 --> 00:21:12.930
What do you mean?

00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:16.830
Well, it's our job to adhere
to the schedule.

00:21:17.530 --> 00:21:24.260
But if it's for you, Mero,
I wouldn't mind reaping that girl's life.

00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:09.330
Meroko! What in the world
were you thinking?

00:23:09.730 --> 00:23:11.500
I can't believe you
would ask Izumi!

00:23:11.930 --> 00:23:16.730
Then what should I have done?!
I don't know what to do anymore.

00:23:17.530 --> 00:23:18.200
Meroko...

00:23:18.600 --> 00:23:20.700
At this rate,
everyone is going to be unhappy.

00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:24.960
I can't stand by and watch anymore!
I hate it! It's all so painful!

